    https://github.com/go-acme/lego
    MIT License
    Used by the Certificate Manager to obtain certificates over ACME.

Vendored browser assets (app/static/vendor/), served locally rather than
from a CDN so that an installation on an isolated management network
renders correctly:

  Chart.js            https://www.chartjs.org/            MIT License
  Bootstrap           https://getbootstrap.com/           MIT License
  Bootstrap Icons     https://icons.getbootstrap.com/     MIT License
  Toast UI Editor     https://ui.toast.com/tui-editor     MIT License
    The Wiki's rich-text editor. Its self-contained build bundles
    ProseMirror (MIT License) and DOMPurify 2.3.3 (Apache License 2.0 or
    Mozilla Public License 2.0, at the user's choice).

The exact versions, the URL each file was taken from and its SHA-256 are in
app/static/vendor/MANIFEST.json; Bootstrap Icons ships its own LICENSE file
next to it.

Rules adapted, not redistributed:

  MDN HTTP Observatory   https://github.com/mdn/mdn-http-observatory
    Mozilla Public License 2.0
    The HTTP Observatory page (app/services/header_observatory.py) applies
    the tests, score modifiers and grade chart of its algorithm version 6 so
    that a site gets the same grade there and in SATOM. The rules were read
    from that project and re-implemented in Python; no file of it is
    included and the descriptions are SATOM's own.

Reference material reproduced:

  The NAF Framework   https://github.com/Network-Automation-Forum/reference
    CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)
    docs/naf-alignment.md maps SATOM to the Network Automation Forum's
    reference model and reproduces its minimal architecture diagram and
    block icons unchanged (docs/img/naf-*.svg, from docs/Framework/images/
    at commit da82b12). CC0 requires no attribution; this notice is given
    anyway, and the framework's brand guidelines are followed.

Python dependencies are declared in requirements.txt and, for offline
